From d3b0ba459e2c4f1312b4e040960470a71d6cb2f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 20:43:23 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 74/81] effect: FBO fit / width / height / uvs, and the swap
 command

WE's effect loader (GH 0x1402131b0) reads an FBO's `scale`, `fit`, `width`, `height` (each a
uint16, taken only up to 4096), `unique`, `clear` and `uvs`; when it allocates them (GH
0x140216080) `width`/`height` replace the layer's size, `fit` caps the longer side keeping the
aspect (the other side truncated), and the result is divided by `scale`. LWE read only scale,
so 3184155462's cursorripple simulation ran its 512-fit buffers at the layer's full size. Now
the size follows WE, also when the layer resizes (text layers). `uvs: "repeat"` (WE's flag 4)
makes the FBO sample wrapping (Inferred: the flag's use wasn't traced).

`command: swap` (WE's command 2, next to copy 1) was refused ("only copy"), which dropped the
stock fluid simulation's ping-pong. It now exchanges the two FBOs' GL storage in place (passes
keep their pointers, so each name reads what the other drew); swaps after the layer's last draw
run after it, outside the chain, so that draw still reaches the scene. Inferred from the stock
use: WE's runtime for command 2 wasn't traced.

Origin: ours
Why: docs/player/spikes/we-coverage.md F9 (fbos.fit, E26)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
